  "narrative": "**Where We Stand**  \nWe sealed the deal with a 3-1 victory over Nepean, putting us atop Pool B with 2 points and advancing us in 65 of 81 remaining tournament scenarios. \n\n**Our Next Game**  \nWe\u2019re right back at it tonight for a battle of pool leaders against the Belmont Blazers on Friday, Oct 16, at 9:15 PM.\n\n**Around the Pool**  \nBelmont enters our matchup fresh off their own tight 2-1 win over Wilmot, while over in Pool A, Ottawa Ice and Woodstock Wildcats each preserved their winning records to round out opening-game action.",
  "coaches_corner": {
    "don_cherry": "I tell ya right now, THAT is how you play Canadian hockey! What did I tell 'em\u2014block shots, clear the crease, and protect that tender, and BOOM, they send Nepean packin' 3-1! Now you got Belmont on deck, so don't you dare let your foot off the gas\u2014keep workin' your socks off and earn that playoff spot, DOUBLE THUMBS UP!",
    "talking_points": "**Mindset**  \nThat 3-1 win over Nepean was a massive statement, but tournament success is about stacking great shifts back-to-back. Bring that same energy, stay hungry, and refuse to get complacent.\n\n**The Opponent**  \nThe Belmont Blazers are also riding high after a tight 2-1 victory over Wilmot, showing they know how to lock down close games and protect a lead. They\u2019re defensively stingy and opportunistic, so we\u2019ll have to fight hard for second-chance pucks in the dirty areas.\n\n**What We Need**  \nWe\u2019re in a fantastic position to claim one of Pool B\u2019s two semifinal spots, but taking control of this game secures our path without leaving anything to chance. Protect our defensive house, drive our goal differential, and let's go take these two points together.",
    "for_game": "Belmont Blazers"
  },
  "tiebreaker_health": "In the 15 score-dependent scenarios, we hold the inside track thanks to our pool-leading +2 GD and tight 1 GA. Belmont sits just behind us at +1 GD (1 GA), meaning even a single-goal swing could trigger deeper tiebreakers. To guarantee we advance through these tiebreaks, we must minimize goals allowed and aim to protect or grow our +1 GD edge over Belmont.",
